														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4838154">
									

<p>OK, so for this one, here's short reasons for why I've downvoted.</p>
<p>First of all, I want to be clear that I don't think your article is bad by any means. You've clearly done work about that, the grammar is perfect and the way you write it is pretty good, I've not really seem something that looked non-clinical or something like that.</p>
<p>But there's two reasons of why I downvote. The first one is the fact that, when I've readed some paragraphs, I've thought at least two times &quot;Wait a minute, that looks like a SCPDeclassified post who weirdly tries to take an in-universe approach&quot; and it felt off-topic at times (Wizz talked about the fact that in the article, 173 is a famous thing and it feels weird).</p>
<p>And the second reason is that, even if it's clear that you've done work and research, the paragraphs and the way it's organized looks like big walls of text, to the point that I had struggle reading that because there was too much words and too much scientific things implied, I was a bit lost.</p>
<p>So, that's why I downvote. But I can see a great lot of potential on your Tale, so I highly suggest you to rework it and pay attention to what others suggested you to do.</p>

							</div>

								
					
